  "method": "Every archived forecast run is compared with what the IMERG satellite later measured for the same cell and day. Brier scores use the run's chance of at least 20 / 40 mm against the observed total; the climatology baseline is that cell's own frequency of such days in the April-November window (the year-months the catalog searched, 2014 onward), and skill = 1 - Brier / Brier_climatology. A medium or high level counts as a warning, scored as hits, misses and false alarms against IMERG >= 40 mm in that cell and against a flood reported within 5 km (the same rule as pipeline/forecast.py). Grouped by lead time, day 1 to day 7. Below 30 scored cell-days for a lead day, enough_data is false.",
